              <h2 class="context-heading">A store you shop by task instead of by product category</h2>
              <p>Disability Design Lab is a concept store for adaptive tools like grips, openers, fasteners and writing aids. <strong>It organizes them by the daily task they help with rather than by product category.</strong> I built it as my midterm for SI 407 at Michigan, against an assigned visual direction of "Experimental &amp; Raw." The catalog and prices are invented. The design system behind them is real.</p>
