          <p class="intro">Adaptive tools are usually sold the way hardware is sold, by category, material and brand. Someone shopping for one starts from a task they can no longer do, like opening a jar, rather than from the name of a product. I designed this for adults whose grip, reach or dexterity has changed, and for the family members and occupational therapists buying on their behalf. I had no user research for this project. I assumed that group skews older and that many of them have some vision loss, so I <strong>designed for low vision reading before I drew anything</strong>. Those are assumptions, and I have labeled them as assumptions everywhere on this page.</p>

